# WatchTell documentation (Divio)

Docs follow https://docs.divio.com/documentation-system/.
Index: `docs/README.md`.

Every page belongs in **exactly one** quadrant:

| Folder | Purpose | Write it as |
|---|---|---|
| `docs/tutorials/` | Learning | A lesson you lead. Concrete steps. Visible result quickly. Minimum theory. |
| `docs/how-to/` | A goal | A recipe. Title works after “How to”. No conceptual essays. |
| `docs/reference/` | Information | Describe the machinery: feature IDs, contracts, architecture, design spec. |
| `docs/explanation/` | Understanding | Why, context, alternatives. No step lists or inventories. |

## Rules

- Do not mix types on one page. Split and link across quadrants.
- Do not add new pages at `docs/*.md`. Use a quadrant folder.
- Update `docs/README.md` when adding or renaming a page.
- Feature inventory stays in `docs/reference/features.md`. Vision, principles, decisions, and roadmap stay in `docs/explanation/`.
- Product language rules still apply in every quadrant.

## Examples

- First-run walkthrough → `docs/tutorials/`
- Adding a watch reference → `docs/how-to/`
- JSON AI contract or report wording → `docs/reference/`
- Why WatchTell does not authenticate → `docs/explanation/`
